# Changesets

A change users of egui_stack notice comes with a changeset: a Markdown
file in this directory, named after the change (`tab-padding.md`). knope
(https://knope.tech) turns the pending changesets into the next version
and its CHANGELOG.md entries at release time (RELEASING.md).

This file has no `.md` extension on purpose: knope reads every `.md`
file here as a changeset.

## Format

```markdown
---
egui_stack: minor
---

`TabStyle` has a new field, `padding`: the space on each side of a tab's
title, `8.0` by default as before.
```

- The front matter is one line: the package, `egui_stack`, and the kind
  of change, `patch`, `minor` or `major`.
- Below it, one paragraph, written for users: it becomes one bullet of
  the changelog. Wrap it as you like, but keep it a single paragraph:
  no heading, no blank line, no wrapped line starting with `-` or `#`.

`knope document-change` asks for the kind and a summary and writes the
file; writing it by hand is as good.

## Which kind

| Kind    | For                                          | Before 1.0           | From 1.0       |
|---------|----------------------------------------------|----------------------|----------------|
| `patch` | a fix                                        | 0.22.1 to 0.22.2     | 1.2.3 to 1.2.4 |
| `minor` | an addition, or a change that breaks nothing | 0.22.1 to 0.22.2     | 1.2.3 to 1.3.0 |
| `major` | a breaking change                            | 0.22.1 to **0.23.0** | 1.2.3 to 2.0.0 |

Before 1.0, a breaking change takes a new middle number, and additions
and fixes share the last one. A changeset still says `major` for a
break: knope applies it to the middle number while the version starts
with 0. Declare what the change is, not the number you expect. The
changelog lists `major` changes under "Breaking changes", `minor` under
"Added" and `patch` under "Fixed".

## Breaking changes: the migration

A `major` changeset ends its paragraph with what a user changes in their
code, in a sentence starting with `Migration:`.

```markdown
---
egui_stack: major
---

`TabViewer::context_menu` gets the tab's `TabPath` instead of its leaf's
`NodePath`, so a menu item can name the tab. Migration: change the last
parameter's type to `TabPath`; `path.node_path()` gives the former
`NodePath`.
```

A break with nothing to change in the code (a new egui version, a higher
minimum Rust version) says so, or names what to bump instead.

## When none is needed

Tests, examples, the documentation, CI and the tooling change nothing
users get. A change in `src/` that users do not notice (a refactoring, a
comment, an internal rename) needs none either: label the pull request
`internal`.

One changeset per change; a pull request doing one thing has one.
